## 1️⃣ Test Way 1: Server-Side Session Persistence (The Core Flaw)
This checks if the logout function only visually logs you out but leaves the session active in the backend database.
## 📋 Step-by-Step Execution

   1. Log into your test account using your main browser window.
   2. Open Burp Suite. Navigate to Proxy -> HTTP history.
   3. Perform a highly sensitive action in the dashboard (e.g., loading the withdrawal screen or changing profile settings).
   4. Find that request in your HTTP history, right-click it, and select Send to Repeater.
   5. Go back to your browser window and click the Logout button normally.
   6. Open Burp Repeater and click Send on the sensitive request you captured in step 3. [1] 

## 🔍 Response Verification Criteria

* Vulnerable Outcome ($1,500 Takeover Path): The server responds with HTTP 200 OK or HTTP 204 No Content and successfully executes the action or returns your private data. This proves the token is still alive in the database.
* Secure Outcome: The server responds with HTTP 401 Unauthorized or HTTP 403 Forbidden.

