## 2️⃣ Test Way 2: Stateless JWT Expiration and Denylist Gaps
Many platforms use JSON Web Tokens (JWTs). Because they are stateless, clicking logout doesn't stop the token from working unless the backend explicitly blocks it.
## 📋 Step-by-Step Execution

   1. Log into your account and open your browser's Developer Tools (F12).
   2. Go to the Application or Storage tab, click Local Storage or Cookies, and copy your active Bearer eyJ... JWT authentication token.
   3. Click Logout on the website.
   4. Open Burp Repeater, construct a manual HTTP request to an API endpoint (e.g., https://1win.com), and insert your copied token header:
   
   Authorization: Bearer <PASTE_YOUR_OLD_JWT_HERE>
   
   5. Wait 5 minutes, 15 minutes, and 30 minutes, clicking Send each time. [2] 

## 🔍 Response Verification Criteria

* Vulnerable Outcome: If the token continues to pull data or perform actions up until its natural cryptographic expiration time (exp claim), the developers failed to implement a server-side denylist.
* To Maximize Payout: Prove that an attacker with this token can immediately change the account password or email address after the victim logged out.

