## 3️⃣ Test Way 3: Multi-Session and Concurrent Device Isolation
This checks if logging out of one active session properly terminates or syncs with other connected clients, or if a global logout is completely broken.
## 📋 Step-by-Step Execution

   1. Open your normal browser tab and log into your account to establish Session A. Copy the session cookie string.
   2. Open an Incognito window and log into the exact same account to establish Session B.
   3. In Session A, click the Logout button.
   4. Switch to your Incognito window (Session B) and attempt to place a bet, make a deposit, or change profile settings.
   5. Alternatively, if the app has a "Log out of all other devices" option, check if old active session tokens captured in Burp still work after triggering it. [3] 

## 🔍 Response Verification Criteria

* Vulnerable Outcome: If Session B remains completely active and can execute trades or modify settings after Session A logged out, the system fails to handle multi-device synchronization or global session revoking.

