## 5️⃣ Test Way 5: Session Token Fixation via Defective Logout Logic
This checks if the application recycles the exact same session tracking ID string before and after the logout event takes place. [4] 
## 📋 Step-by-Step Execution

   1. Open Burp Suite. Log into your test account and note down the precise cookie/token value string (e.g., session_id=XYZ123).
   2. Click the Logout button. Intercept the request to ensure it passes through.
   3. Log right back into the same account, or look at the cookie the browser issues immediately after the logout event. [5, 6] 

## 🔍 Response Verification Criteria

* Vulnerable Outcome: If the application issues the exact same session_id=XYZ123 value after logging out or logging back in, it is vulnerable to session fixation. An attacker who sets that cookie value on a victim's machine before they log in or out will maintain permanent access. [7, 8] 

